From: Richard Fritz <gh@chaos4all.de>
Subject: [PATCH] media: ipu-bridge: Add IMX241 to the list of supported sensors

The Sony IMX241 is found with ACPI HID INT347F on IPU3 based devices
such as the HP Pro x2 612 G2, where it is the front camera on CSI-2
port 1 with 2 data lanes.

Add it to the list of sensors supported by ipu-bridge so that the fwnode
graph is built for it. On this machine the sensor clock comes from the
TPS68470, which also clocks the rear OV8858 and runs at 24 MHz for it.
The imx241 driver then configures a 996 MHz PLL, which gives RAW10 on 2
lanes at 996 Mbit/s per lane, i.e. a link frequency of 498 MHz.

ipu3-cio2 only registers its subdevices once all sensors in the fwnode
graph have bound, so without a driver for the IMX241 this entry would
also make the rear camera unusable on this machine.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Richard Fritz <gh@chaos4all.de>
---
--- a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c
+++ b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c
@@ -71,6 +71,8 @@
 	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("INT347A", 1, 360000000),
 	/* Omnivision OV7251 */
 	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("INT347E", 1, 319200000),
+	/* Sony IMX241 */
+	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("INT347F", 1, 498000000),
 	/* Hynix Hi-556 */
 	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("INT3537", 1, 437000000),
 	/* Lontium lt6911uxe */
